      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General procedure for 1–3: to a stirred MeOH (40 mL) solution of LH4 (0.034 g, 0.1 mmol) and Ln(NO3)3·6H2O (0.075 mmol) was added Et3N (0.013 mL, 0.1 mmol). After 30 min stirring, Cu(ClO4)2·6H2O (0.05 mmol) was added and stirring continued 15 min; further Et3N (0.026 mL, 0.2 mmol) gave a clear brown solution that was stirred at room temperature overnight. Solvent was removed in vacuo; the brown residue was washed 2–3 times with diethyl ether, dried, and dissolved in MeOH/CHCl3 (1:1). Dark brown crystals grew by slow evaporation over ca. 8 d. For 1: LH4 (0.034 g, 0.1 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.034 g, 0.075 mmol), Cu(ClO4)2·6H2O (0.018 g, 0.05 mmol), Et3N (0.039 mL, 0.3 mmol).",
