      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "χmT at 290 K is 41.65 cm3 K mol−1 (two CuII + three DyIII). χmT decreases to a minimum of 38.62 cm3 K mol−1 at 20 K then rises to 41.48 cm3 K mol−1 at 2.2 K, indicating ligand-field depopulation plus weak AF and minor FM exchange. Mm at 2.0 K/5 T is 17.7 NAμB (not saturated). Zero-field ac out-of-phase signals to ca. 12 K; Arrhenius fit 2.0–8.0 K gives τ0 = (2.6 ± 0.1)×10−5 s and Ueff = (5.4 ± 0.1) cm−1 (α 0.29–0.45); SMM-like slow relaxation, not a dominant Orbach process.",
